# Space-separated dynamic-DNS hostnames AND/OR raw IPs whose current
# address(es) always bypass the nftables connection-rate limits (see
# firewall/nftables.conf's trusted_ips set) and can never be banned by any
# fail2ban jail (see fail2ban/jail.local's ignoreip and
# firewall/sync-trusted-source.sh). A raw IP passes through unchanged;
# only hostnames actually get re-resolved on each sync. Placeholder --
# replace with your own admin source(s) before enabling
# sync-trusted-source.timer. Leave empty/unset to disable (both sets stay
# at their static baseline, which is safe -- this is an exemption, not a
# requirement for either mechanism to function).
# Quoting matters: this file is `source`d as a shell script, so an
# unquoted space-separated value parses as a second shell command
# ("command not found") rather than one variable.
TRUSTED_HOSTNAMES="admin.example.com"
